  "details": "# Issue:\n\nWhen starting to Preload a World you will see a little progress bar at the bottom of the World Thumbnail when looking at the World in the \"overview\" of the Worlds Tab.  \n\nThis little progress bar is not correctly being masked though, this results in you being able to see it fly to the side when switching form the Worlds Tab to a different Tab (e.g. Settings)\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**  \n\n1. Start Preloading a World in the Main Menu\n\n2. Go back to the Worlds Tab \"overview\" and find the world you are currently preloading in it  \n\n3. Now switch over to the Settings Tab\n\nIf you do this you will notice the progress bar flying out to the left side of the menu.\n\n# Expected Behavior:  \n\nThe Preload progress bar in the Worlds Tab overview should be properly masked, just like everything else in said Tab is.\n\n# Attachments:  \n\nHere is a video showcasing the issue: \n\nhttps://youtu.be/1K_cHf7eNhc",
